{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence","id":323495,"title":"\"That's not fair! Monsters shouldn't be so smart!\" discussing Lunar Intelligence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-27T01:15:22-08:00","id":323495,"title":"\"That's not fair! Monsters shouldn't be so smart!\" discussing Lunar Intelligence","content":"Okay, so bestial monsters and monstrous beasts, rather than heroes, are the Lunar bailiwick. We actually <i>can </i>work with that for Intelligence Charm inspiration.<br /> <br /> One of the things that scares you about monsters is how &quot;unfair&quot; they are. They're stronger, faster, hardier, armed with more pointy bits, can see in the dark, can track you by scent... Often the only thing that you have in your favor is human intelligence.<br /> <br /> Which makes it all the more terrifying when that advantage is revealed to be smaller than you thought:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ripley:</b> They cut the power.<br /> <b>Hudson:</b> What do you mean, &quot;<i>They</i> cut the power&quot;? How could they cut the power, man? They're animals!&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> I ask you to think back over every horror and survival-action story you've read or watched, and think of times that the monsters displayed a frightful, &quot;animal&quot; cunning. Every time they seemed to learn or understand or anticipate something that it initially didn't seem they could.<br /> <br /> Along with the xenomorphs of <i>Aliens</i>, the velociraptors of <i>Jurassic Park</i> are a great example. It's not the <i>level </i>of their feats (any mortal can figure out a door knob, and Lunars <i>start </i>as mortals), but the <i>kind </i>of feats: Testing defenses and containment measures, looking for a weakness to exploit; Understanding locking mechanisms and how to circumvent them; Discerning resources upon which prey depends, and removing those; Using obscuring terrain, pack tactics, distractions and ambushes. These are the kind of things that Intelligent Lunars accomplish at superhuman levels -- if an animal can learn to use a door knob, a Lunar Exalt could bypass a First Age security lock.<br /> <br /> The titular <i>Predator</i>, despite its arrogance and Arnold's apparent total helplessness, <i>stopped </i>at the last instant by the prompting of some intuition, allowing it to realize that Arnold was baiting it into a trap.<br /> <br /> The Lunars already mimic the monster of <i>The Thing</i> in their ability to take the memories as well as the faces of those they eat. Stealing information that could never have been gained through investigation or torture, and which should have gone to the grave, is a terrifyingly &quot;unfair&quot; ability that forms the stuff of Creation's nightmares.<br /> <br /> It's best to avoid going too far in that field of inspiration, though. The Lunars do not draw inspiration from the Tyranids or Zerg, who rely too heavily on science-fiction in their aesthetic, whereas the Lunar Exalted are supposed to be firmly spirit-and-stone fantasy. Even the resemblance to the The Thing is incidental next to the more down-to-filthy-earth examples of cannibal witch-doctors eating brains as part of their unholy, pagan rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:24:26-08:00","id":323617,"title":"","content":"I feel like Lunars can certainly borrow heavily from StarCraft II Zerg, who are not basically Tyrannic expies (unlike how they were largely portrayed in StarCraft I). Especially with regard to the Zerus/Primal Zerg storyline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:35:35-08:00","id":323623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323617#post323617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Lunars can certainly borrow heavily from StarCraft II Zerg, who are not basically Tyrannic expies (unlike how they were largely portrayed in StarCraft I). Especially with regard to the Zerus/Primal Zerg storyline.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? In what way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:51:44-08:00","id":323630,"title":"","content":"I still wouldn't use The Thing as an inspiration for any Lunar capabilities, because it forms a fundamental part of 2e chimerae, and the more distance from that, the better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323617#post323617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Lunars can certainly borrow heavily from StarCraft II Zerg, who are not basically Tyrannic expies (unlike how they were largely portrayed in StarCraft I). Especially with regard to the Zerus/Primal Zerg storyline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't the Tyranids originally much less like the Zerg of SC1? I seem to recall someone posting unit pictures of what looked like weird looking aliens with swords and &quot;bioguns&quot; on /tg/ of years past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:18:29-08:00","id":323636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323623#post323623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? In what way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Survival of the fittest, planned Darwinism, consuming others to increase your own strength...I wouldn't even mind seeing some of the Darwinian themes in the Silver Pact, like inc your Mentor grows too weak to hold his station you have a duty to overthrow him so the fittest are always in charge. That's just a side thought though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323630#post323630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the Tyranids originally much less like the Zerg of SC1? I seem to recall someone posting unit pictures of what looked like weird looking aliens with swords and &quot;bioguns&quot; on /tg/ of years past.</div> </div> </div> </div>In appearance, sure, nids infantry has always had like bioswords and biorifles etc but then you also have things that are effectively Ultralisks and Mutalisks in everything but name - living tanks, etc. In theme, not really, it was clear that the SC1 Zerg were borrowing heavily from nid themes. SC1 didn't do much with them beyond &quot;giant horde controlled by some specialized conduits for the Overmind,&quot; kind of like the Bugs of Starship Troopers, but I think the Brain Bugs were more independently sentient than anything portrayed in the nids until the Swarmlord, or the Zerg until SC2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:14:08-08:00","id":323664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323636#post323636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival of the fittest, planned Darwinism, consuming others to increase your own strength...I wouldn't even mind seeing some of the Darwinian themes in the Silver Pact, like inc your Mentor grows too weak to hold his station you have a duty to overthrow him so the fittest are always in charge. That's just a side thought though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has no Darwinian themes, and evolutionary fitness has nothing to do with Lunars, seeing as how they don't propagate by blood and both they and beastfolk have many an independent bent away from Pact business (which is pretty much just one thing - fuck the Realm). Even the Social Darwinism that you're bringing up is likely going to end, since it doesn't do much for the asymmetric military goal of EX3 Lunars. You don't want constant infighting in your local cell, or among other cells. It doesn't make them stronger, it just wastes resources while the Realm watches and laughs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In appearance, sure, nids infantry has always had like bioswords and biorifles etc but then you also have things that are effectively Ultralisks and Mutalisks in everything but name - living tanks, etc. In theme, not really, it was clear that the SC1 Zerg were borrowing heavily from nid themes. SC1 didn't do much with them beyond &quot;giant horde controlled by some specialized conduits for the Overmind,&quot; kind of like the Bugs of Starship Troopers, but I think the Brain Bugs were more independently sentient than anything portrayed in the nids until the Swarmlord, or the Zerg until SC2. </div> </div> </div>That's not what sentient means, though in fairness, an awful lot of the &quot;living war machines&quot; of scifi tend to show no indication of feeling pain or discomfort as they crash into mechanical war machines to do battle. Can't really argue too much on the Starcraft vs 40k front, though. I try to stay out of it, so I only catch snippets of arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-27-2014, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:40:01-08:00","id":323671,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of the problem with synthesist summoners in Pathfinder, you can dump your physical stats because you are just going to take them from your Eidalon. I don't thing Lunars necessarily get the stats of their animal forms so hopefully it wont be a problem in EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:59:44-08:00","id":323721,"title":"","content":"I like this model. I think there's room for straight up &quot;uncanny genius&quot; in Lunar Intelligence, but this is a good vision of how to add a distinctive character to them at the tree level.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I tend to imagine Lunars as punishing specialists -- shifting the context of battle into a situation where their adaptability and versatility has the maximum benefit, and exploiting the fact that major adversaries tend to be very narrowly focused. So it's not hard to see them using powers that circumvent or strip away the advantages their opponents rely on, and I could definitely see that sort of thing going in Intelligence, among other places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:36:29-08:00","id":323783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323721#post323721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this model. I think there's room for straight up &quot;uncanny genius&quot; in Lunar Intelligence, but this is a good vision of how to add a distinctive character to them at the tree level.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I tend to imagine Lunars as punishing specialists -- shifting the context of battle into a situation where their adaptability and versatility has the maximum benefit, and exploiting the fact that major adversaries tend to be very narrowly focused. So it's not hard to see them using powers that circumvent or strip away the advantages their opponents rely on, and I could definitely see that sort of thing going in Intelligence, among other places.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you thought you won, you never saw me change the game that we were playing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T12:27:45-08:00","id":323817,"title":"","content":"I like this.<br /> <br /> First off, Chimera are cool, especially as antagonists to regular Lunars, and should be kept around as a concept. Not necessarily implemented the same way, but the idea that a shapeshifter can eventually lose himself and forget who he really is at the core and turn into a monster is really awesome...and Chimera being SMART monsters instead of just ravening beasts makes them amazingly useful for telling horror stories in Exalted. You can definitely have some &quot;it cut off the power?!&quot; moments with Chimera.<br /> <br /> Lunar intelligence should include this sort of cunning. They're guerrilla fighters by nature, so Alien and Predator and other such sneaky badasses make good inspiration even if you don't want your Lunars all alien and transhuman-decent werewolf movies have the same sort of tropes, for instance. Lunars doing things like striking, taking out one member of your group in a chilling display of violence, and vanishing into the night to leave you staring at shadows before striking again days later is definitely in-theme. Lunars taking away your advantages one by one until you're just a big naked ape is also a thing they should be doing: if you have heavy armor, they'll bring the game of cat-and-mouse into a swamp where your armor drags you down into the mud and their scales don't. If you are a brilliant archer, they'll try to get you into a thick jungle. If you're an expert at urban warfare, they'll try to get you out of Chiarascuro into the empty desert, and swim under the sand. They should always be using their amazing versatility to try and take advantage of the fact that you're not as versatile. Like Alien taking advantage of ventilation systems or the fact that nobody ever looks up, they should be intelligently analyzing your weak points and striking you there.<br /> <br /> They are hunters, after all. Every form in their library is something they spent eight hours stalking before killing. There's an intimacy to that sort of hunt: it's about knowing your prey. Lunars should be doing things like figuring out your intimacies by stalking you so they can use them against you, or determining some of your ability ratings during the hunt so they can adapt their tactics to suit your weaknesses. A Lunar hunter should have charms that let them deduce your fears so they can become them, or to figure out who you trust so they can devour the heart of someone who can get them close to you. If you're another exalt, you're dangerous, so they'll take their time: being hunted by a Lunar exalt shouldn't just be a big furry monster tearing out of the woods: you should KNOW you're being hunted, and be TERRIFIED of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T13:32:54-08:00","id":323841,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... A simplification like &quot;Lunar Intelligence Charms are not monstruous on their own... but are particularly intimidating within the body of a monster&quot;? Complementary mental abilities to enhance the effect of their primary physical changing (mental because these examples work as well for Perception and Wits). Probably a horrible simplification.<br /> <br /> Definitely one sort of cool inspiration to consider. Although I don't know if Lunars, chimera apart are ever really &quot;it&quot;, rather than just perceived that way by prey (when that suits the Lunar), and a new idea. Of course, Lunars need to have Intelligence beyond the predatory, as they can't just be &quot;terrifying&quot; or predators and hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T16:00:13-08:00","id":323936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323817#post323817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, Chimera are cool, especially as antagonists to regular Lunars, and should be kept around as a concept. Not necessarily implemented the same way, but the idea that a shapeshifter can eventually lose himself and forget who he really is at the core and turn into a monster is really awesome...and Chimera being SMART monsters instead of just ravening beasts makes them amazingly useful for telling horror stories in Exalted. You can definitely have some &quot;it cut off the power?!&quot; moments with Chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a real issue with the notion that of all the Exalted, only Lunars might risk losing themselves and basically turning into the Relic as a side-cost of <i>actually using their native powers</i>. This should be a thing that happens to all of them or to none. Losing control of your body and mind for constantly being something you are not (which is one of your bred-and-butter powers on top of it) is just punitive when layered on top of the Great Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T16:04:04-08:00","id":323939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323817#post323817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this.<br /> <br /> First off, Chimera are cool, especially as antagonists to regular Lunars, and should be kept around as a concept. Not necessarily implemented the same way, but the idea that a shapeshifter can eventually lose himself and forget who he really is at the core and turn into a monster is really awesome...and Chimera being SMART monsters instead of just ravening beasts makes them amazingly useful for telling horror stories in Exalted. You can definitely have some &quot;it cut off the power?!&quot; moments with Chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you won't. At least, no more so than any other Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cromage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: I like the idea of &quot;dualism&quot; but I'm not so keen on the &quot;human vs monster&quot; and have actually seen that more in the province of (gasp!) other splats (don't kill me). I like the idea of Lunars being champions of two worlds--exiles, outsiders, emigrants, and wanderers--and having to either choose one world or another or somehow trying to reconcile them.</i><br /> <i>ETA: More importantly I always hated chimerism and its tendency to drag Lunars into really dumb places. Maybe 3e will make it not suck.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A: Human vs. monster isn't on the schedule. I'm not turning Lunars into a werewolf story.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Chimeraism is going to be way different in EX3.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunar intelligence should include this sort of cunning. They're guerrilla fighters by nature, so Alien and Predator and other such sneaky badasses make good inspiration even if you don't want your Lunars all alien and transhuman-decent werewolf movies have the same sort of tropes, for instance. Lunars doing things like striking, taking out one member of your group in a chilling display of violence, and vanishing into the night to leave you staring at shadows before striking again days later is definitely in-theme. Lunars taking away your advantages one by one until you're just a big naked ape is also a thing they should be doing: if you have heavy armor, they'll bring the game of cat-and-mouse into a swamp where your armor drags you down into the mud and their scales don't. If you are a brilliant archer, they'll try to get you into a thick jungle. If you're an expert at urban warfare, they'll try to get you out of Chiarascuro into the empty desert, and swim under the sand. They should always be using their amazing versatility to try and take advantage of the fact that you're not as versatile. Like Alien taking advantage of ventilation systems or the fact that nobody ever looks up, they should be intelligently analyzing your weak points and striking you there.<br /> <br /> They are hunters, after all. Every form in their library is something they spent eight hours stalking before killing. There's an intimacy to that sort of hunt: it's about knowing your prey. Lunars should be doing things like figuring out your intimacies by stalking you so they can use them against you, or determining some of your ability ratings during the hunt so they can adapt their tactics to suit your weaknesses. A Lunar hunter should have charms that let them deduce your fears so they can become them, or to figure out who you trust so they can devour the heart of someone who can get them close to you. If you're another exalt, you're dangerous, so they'll take their time: being hunted by a Lunar exalt shouldn't just be a big furry monster tearing out of the woods: you should KNOW you're being hunted, and be TERRIFIED of it. </div> </div> </div>&quot;They cut the geomantic power flow!&quot; is probably more likely due to Perception (to sense how the Essence flow in a Manse moves with a sensitivity for the mystical) and Strength (to &quot;redecorate&quot; the Manse by turning into a bull and rampaging around all of the sculptures and fine china). Intelligence probably sees more use in vision quests, omen reading, dream interpretation, and producing toxins and other substances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T18:34:12-08:00","id":324032,"title":"","content":"Something that is important to remember... Lunars are people. They couple human brilliance with animal instinct and cunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T19:04:47-08:00","id":324043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324032#post324032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that is important to remember... Lunars are people. They couple human brilliance with animal instinct and cunning.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence#post323495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along with the xenomorphs of <i>Aliens</i>, the velociraptors of <i>Jurassic Park</i> are a great example. It's not the <i>level </i>of their feats (<b>any mortal can figure out a door knob, and Lunars <i>start </i>as mortals</b>), but the <i>kind </i>of feats: Testing defenses and containment measures, looking for a weakness to exploit; Understanding locking mechanisms and how to circumvent them; Discerning resources upon which prey depends, and removing those; Using obscuring terrain, pack tactics, distractions and ambushes. These are the kind of things that Intelligent Lunars accomplish at superhuman levels -- <b>if an animal can learn to use a door knob, a Lunar Exalt could bypass a First Age security lock</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you quoted no one and don't seem to be responding to Saur Ops, I must conclude that you are responding to the original post.<br /> <br /> In which case, I think you skipped something.<br /> <br /> I get very angry when people skim my words and post a point they think I overlooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T19:37:19-08:00","id":324104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324043#post324043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since you quoted no one and don't seem to be responding to Saur Ops, I must conclude that you are responding to the original post.<br /> <br /> In which case, I think you skipped something.<br /> <br /> I get very angry when people skim my words and post a point they think I overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright then. I'm sorry you are angry. Of course, if my agreeing with you makes you angry, I will bow out of the conversation, before I do something that REALLY makes you angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T19:44:06-08:00","id":324150,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if you feel as insulted as I felt, but &quot;Something to remember&quot; suggests that no one has remembered it. You quoted no one, and nothing in your post was worded to affirm someone else's stated points.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323664#post323664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has no Darwinian themes, and evolutionary fitness has nothing to do with Lunars, seeing as how they don't propagate by blood and both they and beastfolk have many an independent bent away from Pact business (which is pretty much just one thing - fuck the Realm). Even the Social Darwinism that you're bringing up is likely going to end, since it doesn't do much for the asymmetric military goal of EX3 Lunars. You don't want constant infighting in your local cell, or among other cells. It doesn't make them stronger, it just wastes resources while the Realm watches and laughs.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Saur ops said, Zel.<br /> <br /> Slim chance of Zerg or Tyranids in our Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T21:11:49-08:00","id":324196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324043#post324043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since you quoted no one and don't seem to be responding to Saur Ops, I must conclude that you are responding to the original post.<br /> <br /> In which case, I think you skipped something.<br /> <br /> I get very angry when people skim my words and post a point they think I overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, the internet. Ate my last post, I see. I apologize for upsetting you. Without the emphasis of actual speech, I can understand that you read that is deliberately insulting, rather than agreeing with you. I was on my phone, and making proper, well-thought out posts is difficult on a small keyboard, especially when switching trains.<br /> <br /> The point I would have liked to make is fairly straightforward: Lunar brilliance should exceed everyone's. Lunars have moments of brilliance far beyond what mortals or animals can do, and it is not because of either. The Ability Excellency allows them to combine the momentary insight of an instinctual creature with the long term learning of an aged and learned individual.<br /> <br /> Still, seeing as how I've upset you, I shall bow out of the conversation. I would only recommend that you try to leap to understanding rather than anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T21:54:53-08:00","id":324223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323664#post323664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Social Darwinism that you're bringing up is likely going to end, since it doesn't do much for the asymmetric military goal of EX3 Lunars. You don't want constant infighting in your local cell, or among other cells. It doesn't make them stronger, it just wastes resources while the Realm watches and laughs.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324150#post324150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Saur ops said, Zel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be disappointed if the Pact remains something of a monolith, guerrilla war or no. Not every Lunar is going to give a shit about participating in it after all (until the Sidereals/Realm forces them to, of course!) <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T23:00:26-08:00","id":324232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324223#post324223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be disappointed if the Pact remains something of a monolith, guerrilla war or no. Not every Lunar is going to give a shit about participating in it after all (until the Sidereals/Realm forces them to, of course!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that it's going to be rather loose in structure, and that most Lunars participate because they don't want to die, the Realm is hemming them in and in the way of their personal plans, and because one Lunar isn't going to fell such a giant organization on her own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T02:31:03-08:00","id":324331,"title":"","content":"I can see Lunars as carrying the uncanny image of the bestial monster that can apply problem solving skills, but that would appear to be emergent from the fact that they're shapeshifters more than Charms.<br /> <br /> I mean, I suppose one could make shapeshifting something that inhibits a Lunar's rationality for the sake of then having Intelligence Charms to let them use their full mind in other forms, but that strikes me as a bit of an air-breathing mermaid thing.<br /> <br /> I do have this image now in which a Lunar is incongruously standing as the sole human figure amidst a bunch of beasts, and the presence and direction of the Lunar gives them an out-of-sorts level of coordination and deliberation; it's an image distinct from being a trainer, more like... being Nymeria the dire wolf in terms of her effect on her terrifyingly massive pack. Even some portrayals of Tarzan.<br /> <br /> I could see Intelligence Charms following the idea that the Lunar is able to warp their own perspective and mental processes so that they can fit their planning and directing activity into a pattern that is significantly different from their usual default; it's like, the Lunar didn't elevate the animals (or people of a certain particularly idiosyncratic culture), they just distilled themselves into a form that could communicate ideas that would prompt responses from which the desired result is an emergent property.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T02:36:28-08:00","id":324333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324223#post324223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be disappointed if the Pact remains something of a monolith, guerrilla war or no. Not every Lunar is going to give a shit about participating in it after all (until the Sidereals/Realm forces them to, of course!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're going to get a significant number of Lunars who are only casually interested in the thing, or even have a degree of friction against it, but they're still caught up in its orbit because the most powerful Lunars are at the heart of it, they have done Lunar things that many others are still likely to find <i>impressive</i> (I'd look at Seven Devil Clever in that preview fiction), and the more invested Lunars are advertising the networking opportunities inherent to it.<br /> <br /> That last one is to say, if you're a young Lunar with no interest in fighting the Realm, but you still have interests in which the aid or significant accumulated resources of other Lunars can help, then some actions against the Realm can be the currency in which you pay for those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T02:37:33-08:00","id":324334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324331#post324331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I suppose one could make shapeshifting something that inhibits a Lunar's rationality for the sake of then having Intelligence Charms to let them use their full mind in other forms, but that strikes me as a bit of an air-breathing mermaid thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought it should be more a Dragon King thing in recognition of the fact that being more bestial for them is a step backwards in their personal evolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T10:18:14-08:00","id":324624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324196#post324196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point I would have liked to make is fairly straightforward: Lunar brilliance should exceed everyone's. Lunars have moments of brilliance far beyond what mortals or animals can do, and it is not because of either. The Ability Excellency allows them to combine the momentary insight of an instinctual creature with the long term learning of an aged and learned individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads back to the more general problem of Lunar potential and what it actually translates to. Given that a Solar will always be better at X where X is some task defined by an ability and that all such tasks have an attribute attached to them, what does it mean that Lunars brilliant than Solars (or whatever else) when the Solar will still have the better thought out arguments (Int+Lore) the more acute observations (Per+Invest), etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T11:59:44-08:00","id":324712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324624#post324624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This leads back to the more general problem of Lunar potential and what it actually translates to. Given that a Solar will always be better at X where X is some task defined by an ability and that all such tasks have an attribute attached to them, what does it mean that Lunars brilliant than Solars (or whatever else) when the Solar will still have the better thought out arguments (Int+Lore) the more acute observations (Per+Invest), etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is supposed to be that the smart (high-Int) Lunar is going to be able to do things just with Int Charms that the Solar would need Lore, Occult, Medicine, etc. to do. Less need to spread around, because Attributes are so broad already.<br /> <br /> In theory this works; in practice, this point is frequently moot. Unless Int Charms are written more broadly such that one Charm can be applicable to thinking about all of Lore, Occult, and Medicine, versus having an Int Charm focused on Lore stuff, another focused on Occult stuff, etc. The latter is more of what previous editions gave us: Ability Charm specificity but just using a different trait as min.<br /> <br /> What I'm hoping is that since Attributes are broader than Abilities, Attribute Charms will be more broadly applicable, i.e. a Charisma Charm will be useful with Presence, Performance, Socialize, Investigation, etc. Some Lunar stuff did this (not much) but IIRC Alchemical stuff was on point for broadness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T14:23:43-08:00","id":324783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323936#post323936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a real issue with the notion that of all the Exalted, only Lunars might risk losing themselves and basically turning into the Relic as a side-cost of <i>actually using their native powers</i>. This should be a thing that happens to all of them or to none. Losing control of your body and mind for constantly being something you are not (which is one of your bred-and-butter powers on top of it) is just punitive when layered on top of the Great Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, who said only Lunars lose themselves?<br /> <br /> Solars lose themselves in their power and become mad god-tyrants, forgetting over time what it's like to be human and justifying ever-grander atrocities and extremes of harmful virtue.<br /> Sidereals lose themselves in &quot;the greater good&quot; and slowly sacrifice the things that they use to define themselves to Fate, and hope they can pull enough strings to make the cost worth it.<br /> Infernals lose themselves in transcendent alien power, becoming less and less human and more and more a cosmic monster until their alien principles matter more than their former lives.<br /> Dragonbloods lose themselves in politics and power, giving up who they are for their families in the hope that someday they'll be the powerful Elder and retain enough of who they are to fix things.<br /> Abyssal loyalists lose themselves in hateful nihilism, and rebellious ones know they've already lost what matters and are trying to regain it.<br /> Alchemicals lose themselves in service to the state and the Maker, at constant risk of letting Clarity and logic override their hopes and dreams.<br /> <br /> Lunars losing themselves in foreign shapes, forgetting who they really are underneath all the masks, is just their particular way of doing it.<br /> <br /> One of the central themes of Exalted is having tremendous world-shaping power and trying to remain true to who you are and do something that matters to you, hopefully something good, with all that power. Losing yourself amidst all that power is a core Exalted story, like an Aberrant losing themselves amidst celebrity or a Vampire losing herself to the Beast or a Noble losing himself as he merged with his Estate. The Exalted are virtuous humans struggling to remain virtuous given the powers of the gods themselves, and many of them fail and become divine horrors. That's a central theme of the game, and I'd hate to lose it.<br /> <br /> Now, I certainly don't want it to be something that's rubbed in your face constantly? Like, your PCs shouldn't worry about chimerism constantly unless that's the sort of game you're all up for playing, it should be something that happens in extreme cases? But I always felt that the Green Lady has always been steppin' on some Lunar themes about identity.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about the Earthsea books, where Ged turns into a hawk and stays in the shape too long and almost forgets he was ever a man. Those are some potent themes! We should be careful with their use, but I'd hate to lose them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T14:37:04-08:00","id":324789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324624#post324624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This leads back to the more general problem of Lunar potential and what it actually translates to. Given that a Solar will always be better at X where X is some task defined by an ability and that all such tasks have an attribute attached to them, what does it mean that Lunars brilliant than Solars (or whatever else) when the Solar will still have the better thought out arguments (Int+Lore) the more acute observations (Per+Invest), etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For one thing, you might have Lunars who can do pretty well at Lore or Investigation even if their personalities and inclinations don't have you build them with a single dot in either.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm going to think that looking at Lunars in terms of doing things generically well rather than doing them with varying degrees of force that make them feel like Lunars is going to be disappointed from the outset.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have distinctive Investigation and Lore magic without being the absolute best investigators and scholars. Lunars will certainly be more different still in how the things they do aren't oriented around an aesthetic rendering of some particular skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T14:55:36-08:00","id":324798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=323936#post323936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a real issue with the notion that of all the Exalted, only Lunars might risk losing themselves and basically turning into the Relic as a side-cost of <i>actually using their native powers</i>. This should be a thing that happens to all of them or to none.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it shouldn't, no more than there should be any generic Exalted competence.<br /> <br /> Still, Liminals are going to have their own form of identity issues, including those that stem from swapping around body parts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T15:03:22-08:00","id":324814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324789#post324789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, you might have Lunars who can do pretty well at Lore or Investigation even if their personalities and inclinations don't have you build them with a single dot in either.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm going to think that looking at Lunars in terms of doing things generically well rather than doing them with varying degrees of force that make them feel like Lunars is going to be disappointed from the outset.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have distinctive Investigation and Lore magic without being the absolute best investigators and scholars. Lunars will certainly be more different still in how the things they do aren't oriented around an aesthetic rendering of some particular skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it: bingo. There will be places where Lunar Charms pull off broader effects than Solar Charms do. Where this happens, I get the feeling it will be less a matter of Lunar Charms just being broader and more that this emerges naturally from whatever powers the Charms are trying to evoke. Again, where this happens. I expect there to be plenty of Lunar Charms that are roughly as broad or narrow as Solar ones. They'll just be pointed in different directions than Solar Charms would, or approaching similar directions through different avenues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T15:08:19-08:00","id":324822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324783#post324783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking about the Earthsea books, where Ged turns into a hawk and stays in the shape too long and almost forgets he was ever a man. Those are some potent themes! We should be careful with their use, but I'd hate to lose them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just me, my response to this was that I find that more interesting if it's psychologically motivated rather than a consequence of using Lunar power. If you lose yourself in a hawk, its because psychologically you have something in you which wants or needs that. I'm not sure that can fit that easily into mechanics. Maybe if the mechanics are correct or it may not be better to mechanize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T15:42:19-08:00","id":324835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324822#post324822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just me, my response to this was that I find that more interesting if it's psychologically motivated rather than a consequence of using Lunar power. If you lose yourself in a hawk, its because psychologically you have something in you which wants or needs that. I'm not sure that can fit that easily into mechanics. Maybe if the mechanics are correct or it may not be better to mechanize.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, or it's an example of using shapeshifting sorcery rather than a consequence of Lunar shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T16:26:51-08:00","id":324842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324798#post324798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it shouldn't, no more than there should be any generic Exalted competence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty bullshit if one or two of the major splats have &quot;lose control of Self as a byproduct of using our native powers&quot; issues, above and beyond the Great Curse, and none of the other splats do.<br /> Heavy stick mechanics like 2e Lunar Chimerism and Sidereal Paradox don't do anything except punish splat choice and utilizing intended splat powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324822#post324822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just me, my response to this was that I find that more interesting if it's psychologically motivated rather than a consequence of using Lunar power. If you lose yourself in a hawk, its because psychologically you have something in you which wants or needs that. I'm not sure that can fit that easily into mechanics. Maybe if the mechanics are correct or it may not be better to mechanize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you could do mechanics for this and not present it like an Animorphs style balancing stick. That was a fundamental limitation that characters knew in-setting and broke, after all.<br /> <br /> Maybe the best way to model it is with Intimacies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-28-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T17:04:29-08:00","id":324867,"title":"","content":"I prefer pushing that further. Not, &quot;this enemy is powerful and deadly and also cunning&quot; but instead &quot;this enemy is so cunning it doesn't matter that we are more powerful and deadly&quot;. An enemy that can out think and out plan the players, and I mean legitimately not metagaming information he shouldn't have access to. They know how to get inside your head and manipulate you. The reason I find this so effective is your average player is taken far out of their comfort zone. Unlike the OP idea of a monster thats completely superior there is a certain comfort in confronting your enemy. ultimately that monster intends to fight you. But take that away, an enemy that can't beat you in a fight will keep himself out of your reach. Mess with the psyche of the players, erode their sense of security and make them turn on each other. Best part is this removes that annoying issue of players killing an antagonist before he can get his plans going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T17:27:02-08:00","id":324896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324842#post324842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty bullshit if one or two of the major splats have &quot;lose control of Self as a byproduct of using our native powers&quot; issues, above and beyond the Great Curse, and none of the other splats do.<br /> Heavy stick mechanics like 2e Lunar Chimerism and Sidereal Paradox don't do anything except punish splat choice and utilizing intended splat powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <i>that </i>out there, really. It may not be innate, but Wyld-Shaping is one of the most iconic, splat-defining Solar powers, and it can explode in your face in an absolutely catastrophic way. Sidereals have always had to contend with Paradox and the Curse at the same time, even if initially their Curse had no mechanical representation. Alchemical Clarity has substantial, unpleasant drawbacks. And so forth! Obviously the ratio of carrot to stick is pretty important. I don't think I'd make an actual &quot;roll to remember you're not a hawk&quot; mechanic without a pretty compelling reason. But I could see something <i>like</i> that being in the game without finding it a problem.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T19:54:51-08:00","id":324987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324896#post324896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not <i>that </i>out there, really. It may not be innate, but Wyld-Shaping is one of the most iconic, splat-defining Solar powers, and it can explode in your face in an absolutely catastrophic way. Sidereals have always had to contend with Paradox and the Curse at the same time, even if initially their Curse had no mechanical representation. Alchemical Clarity has substantial, unpleasant drawbacks. And so forth! Obviously the ratio of carrot to stick is pretty important. I don't think I'd make an actual &quot;roll to remember you're not a hawk&quot; mechanic without a pretty compelling reason. But I could see something <i>like</i> that being in the game without finding it a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of those things is not like the other, given that Alchemical native charms either require (or impose but it comes to the same thing) a certain level of clarity or function better with it.<br /> <br /> There were a few good chimera knacks, but they weren't basic to Lunar powers the way clarity was.<br /> <br /> (I like the Clarity method better, or something like Earth Scorpion's explanation for capbreakers as being derived from the great curse)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T20:30:10-08:00","id":325024,"title":"","content":"Lunars would make rather poor antagonists to Sidereals, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded if they were dumb.<br /> <br /> I prefer cunning to smart, but that's because I want the trickster elements of the splat to be as prominent as the raging beast and sexy predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T22:46:14-08:00","id":325104,"title":"","content":"If you want a Lunar Intelligence charm set, rather than physically shifting their bodies, have them shift a mentality which in turn gives them a bonus.<br /> <br /> Consider that Hannibal Lector displays a great deal of traits associated with Lunars, especially elder lunars. He loves the hunt, he considers himself a refined monster, he eats his prey, he camouflages his true nature in public to better stalk his quarry and he tends to defeat his foes by out planning them rather than out fighting them.<br /> <br /> The mind is the most adaptable part of our bodies, which in turn makes it our most powerful weapon. Yet the Lunars seem stuck in the concept that only the body can change while the mind stays intact with the exception of limit break issues.<br /> <br /> Though we have to be honest that in the end a charm bonus or ability is still just that. So the fluff and mechanics for it have to be very carefully worded, lest people just start saying the charms are copy &amp; paste of a different splat. Or in the case of 2nd Edition Lunars, just saying &quot;solar core page x&quot; to save on word count.<br /> <br /> For instance take the Solar charm &quot;Know the Soul's Price&quot;, which allows you to understand what a given PC or NPC will break their morals to achieve (being bribed or what they desire most, etc). Well a Lunar charm could do the exact same thing, but the wording would have to reflect the fact that everything breaks down to animalistic/basic terms. So rather than talking about bribery or a desired goal, the charm would let the Lunar know the target wants a mate, desires security or wishes to outdo a rival, etc., etc.<br /> <br /> This goes back to the idea that to understand a thing, you know what it is capable of. This in turn allows you to hunt your prey successfully.<br /> <br /> In truth so much of our modern world can be broken down into a half dozen or so basic drives &amp; concepts, the rest is just fluff. In short Lunars and their charm set should be about tossing the fluff and working with basics.<br /> <br /> It's not that a person really wants gold (inedible, too soft and rare to make a shelter, too heavy for clothes, etc) but what they want is what gold represents, which is a medium to trade for all those things if they don't have them. A Lunar scoffs at the notion because they can just adjust themselves on the fly, but this means they would not value the equipment that gold would buy nor the gold itself.<br /> <br /> Now just scale that mentality to deal with artifacts, empires or religion and that is a good place to start with Lunars. Admittedly such a play style would mostly likely be a tad bit too philosophical for many people, so it might not work out so well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T23:02:39-08:00","id":325110,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of discussion about whether this idea is valid at all, but not many examples from horror movies being offered like I hoped.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any other horrifying kinds of animal cunning to share? Again, the <i>level</i> of the accomplish matters less than the <i>kind</i>, since Exalted take things over the top. Turtles have hard shells, but Lunars would have harder shells than any mortal turtle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324196#post324196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, the internet. Ate my last post, I see. I apologize for upsetting you. Without the emphasis of actual speech, I can understand that you read that is deliberately insulting, rather than agreeing with you. I was on my phone, and making proper, well-thought out posts is difficult on a small keyboard, especially when switching trains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also know how frustrating and sometimes impossible it is to properly convey one's thoughts on this forum when posting from a smart phone. (And I'd already had to deal with someone recently who clearly didn't have that excuse, on another forum.)<br /> <br /> If that was the problem, then your apology is accepted, I offer my own, and I hope we can move past this unpleasantness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point I would have liked to make is fairly straightforward: Lunar brilliance should exceed everyone's. </div> </div> </div>Going to have to reject this idea out of hand, because it describes the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> The point of this thread is exploring the idea that Lunar Exalted take the cunning of monsters to supernatural levels, such as the particular examples from literature and movies. Whether or not anyone believes that will or should be the case seems off-topic to me, and I would appreciate it that argument could be taken to another thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324331#post324331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Lunars as carrying the uncanny image of the bestial monster that can apply problem solving skills, but that would appear to be emergent from the fact that they're shapeshifters more than Charms.<br /> <br /> I mean, I suppose one could make shapeshifting something that inhibits a Lunar's rationality for the sake of then having Intelligence Charms to let them use their full mind in other forms, but that strikes me as a bit of an air-breathing mermaid thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed the &quot;animal figures out door-knob, Lunar figures out First Age security lock&quot; part of the original post.<br /> <br /> The Lunar starts at the human level of intelligence, and then (represented by Charms) reaches superhuman intelligence in the areas where animals seem to reach basic human intelligence. Put another way, the ways in which animals are cunning are the ways in which Lunars can be as brilliant as Solar Exalted (as represented by Investigation and Lore Charms).<br /> <br /> Other Exalted cannot count on creating an environment, system, plan or weapon that Lunars cannot navigate, circumvent, sabotage, destroy, or subvert. This cunning would naturally be represented with Charms and would not be at all impacted by what form a Lunar currently happens to be wearing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324789#post324789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, you might have Lunars who can do pretty well at Lore or Investigation even if their personalities and inclinations don't have you build them with a single dot in either.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm going to think that looking at Lunars in terms of doing things generically well rather than doing them with varying degrees of force that make them feel like Lunars is going to be disappointed from the outset.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have distinctive Investigation and Lore magic without being the absolute best investigators and scholars. Lunars will certainly be more different still in how the things they do aren't oriented around an aesthetic rendering of some particular skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And one of the ways the Sidereals are distinctive is the way in which they <i>cannot</i> investigate or study things the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'm proposing a way in which Lunars can be magically smart which includes a way in which they <i>cannot</i> be magically smart. Because there are some Charm concepts for which &quot;animal cunning&quot; simply do not properly apply. In some of those areas, Lunars can fill in with other inspirations, like &quot;cannibal shamans eating brains in pagan rituals&quot; and other &quot;barbarian bush magic&quot; acts that Solar Charms would never mimic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=324867#post324867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer pushing that further. Not, &quot;this enemy is powerful and deadly and also cunning&quot; but instead &quot;this enemy is so cunning it doesn't matter that we are more powerful and deadly&quot;. An enemy that can out think and out plan the players, and I mean legitimately not metagaming information he shouldn't have access to. They know how to get inside your head and manipulate you. The reason I find this so effective is your average player is taken far out of their comfort zone. Unlike the OP idea of a monster thats completely superior there is a certain comfort in confronting your enemy. ultimately that monster intends to fight you. But take that away, an enemy that can't beat you in a fight will keep himself out of your reach. Mess with the psyche of the players, erode their sense of security and make them turn on each other. Best part is this removes that annoying issue of players killing an antagonist before he can get his plans going.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're agreeing with me.<br /> <br /> It's not like Full Moons are No Moons, or vice versa. You're going to have Lunars who are one or the other rather than both, especially the young ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-29-2014, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T01:23:09-08:00","id":325143,"title":"","content":"Speaking for myself, I feel like my doubts about your idea are only like:<br /> <br /> a) whether the same &quot;horror movie monster&quot; effect exactly works if your baseline is that the monster is fully human and goes beyond human in specific ways, rather than an &quot;it&quot; that is just an animal that eerily can think beyond its level. the meme seems to exploit the idea that humans are surprised by being stripped of an advantage they thought they held over a predatory natural world... but Lunars don't really represent that predatory world and are expected to be at least human in their intellect.<br /> <br /> b) whether Lunar Intelligence should be specifically predatory or terrifying. I kind of like the idea of it being inspiring and beautiful as well. I don't have much interest in that terrifying predator side of the Lunars.<br /> <br /> While I don't think it's big enough for their intelligence or has quite the same effect it does with a horror film monster, I could probably see Lunars having a &quot;Cunning predator&quot; Charm pattern within Intelligence (or all their Mental Attributes) though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T08:37:39-08:00","id":325306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=325143#post325143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking for myself, I feel like my doubts about your idea are only like:<br /> <br /> a) whether the same &quot;horror movie monster&quot; effect exactly works if your baseline is that the monster is fully human and goes beyond human in specific ways, rather than an &quot;it&quot; that is just an animal that eerily can think beyond its level. the meme seems to exploit the idea that humans are surprised by being stripped of an advantage they thought they held over a predatory natural world... but Lunars don't really represent that predatory world and are expected to be at least human in their intellect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charms aren't competing against the abilities of mortal humans. Lunar Charms are competing against the Charms of other Exalted.<br /> <br /> Solars are the human heroes, and Lunars are the bestial heroes. It makes sense that a Solar (or Terrestrial or Sidereal) would be shocked that bestial power can make Lunars <i>smarter</i> as well as stronger... and as smart as the Solar himself, who is smarter than any other human! And just imagine an Alchemical's horror that flesh and blood alone can do that, when their reality is about the weakness of flesh and the power of metal and wire and lightning.<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't animals, but it's too easy for other Exalted to mistake them for such. In a way, just as it was easy for the marines to dismiss the idea that the xenomorphs might be puzzle-solving smart just because they were animals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) whether Lunar Intelligence should be specifically predatory or terrifying. I kind of like the idea of it being inspiring and beautiful as well. I don't have much interest in that terrifying predator side of the Lunars. </div> </div> </div>Why must Lunar Intelligence be strictly one or the other? Why can't Lunars draw upon the predator side even if it's an area of Charms you wouldn't purchase for your characters?<br /> <br /> Besides, &quot;animal cunning&quot; also includes things like &quot;build webs, dams, nests, [shelter]&quot;. That could be one of the things that Lunars can do at superhuman levels, precisely because it's a thing that both humans and animals do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could probably see Lunars having a &quot;Cunning predator&quot; Charm pattern within Intelligence (or all their Mental Attributes) though. </div> </div> </div>There you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-29-2014, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T16:57:00-08:00","id":325648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=325306#post325306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense that a Solar (or Terrestrial or Sidereal) would be shocked that bestial power can make Lunars <i>smarter</i> as well as stronger...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the hell would that be shocking in the least? If the Lunar has only appeared to be - and acted like - an unassuming animal not noted for its intellect this whole time, maybe, but once the Lunar outs himself as a being of even close to human intellect, let alone as a Lunar, there's no reason to expect that.<br /> <br /> In short, a giant slug opens a door, somewhat unnerving. A raven opens a door? They figure that sort of shit out <i>all the time</i>. A human opens the door? I'm not gonna bat an eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026and as smart as the Solar himself, who is smarter than any human! </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see, you're going with &quot;only Exalts with a three-dot specialty in Hubris need apply.&quot; Feh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars aren't animals, but it's too easy for other Exalted to mistake them for such. </div> </div> </div>Do you even <i>like</i> Lunars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a way, just as it was easy for the marines to dismiss the idea that the xenomorphs\u2026 </div> </div> </div>A class of being who did <i>not</i> have an entire religious order spreading information about it and its deadly cunning for thousands of years\u2026 and thus an irrelevant example. <br /> <br /> I'm gonna go back to my ravens example. Ravens are smart. They can not only figure out tricks like bending a wire into a book to get a treat from a long-necked bottle, they can <i>teach each other tricks</i>. They can see our technology and use it to their benefit (dropping nuts in the crosswalk for cars to crack, then hitting the &quot;PRESS TO CROSS&quot; button to fly down and pick up their treat).<br /> <br /> We know ravens are smart. The scary thing about a raven-turned-serial-killer isn't that it's smart, because we knew that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T17:11:13-08:00","id":325655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=325648#post325648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I see, you're going with &quot;only Exalts with a three-dot specialty in Hubris need apply.&quot; Feh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best integrity specialty. Gotta remember that for later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:27:17-08:00","id":328834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=325110#post325110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I also know how frustrating and sometimes impossible it is to properly convey one's thoughts on this forum when posting from a smart phone. (And I'd already had to deal with someone recently who clearly didn't have that excuse, on another forum.)<br /> <br /> If that was the problem, then your apology is accepted, I offer my own, and I hope we can move past this unpleasantness.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your apology is accepted, but I still think I shall remove myself permanently from these forums. I've come to the conclusion that there really isn't very much for me here anymore, at least until 3rd comes out, and the Monday Meeting notes covers what I want from that. I do thank everyone for stimulating conversation and interesting ideas, and news of 3rd Ed, which originally brought me here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T22:31:24-08:00","id":330765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=325648#post325648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the hell would that be shocking in the least? If the Lunar has only appeared to be - and acted like - an unassuming animal not noted for its intellect this whole time, maybe, but once the Lunar outs himself as a being of even close to human intellect, let alone as a Lunar, there's no reason to expect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're glossing over the difference between mortal human intelligence and Exalted human intelligence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, a giant slug opens a door, somewhat unnerving. A raven opens a door? They figure that sort of shit out <i>all the time</i>. A human opens the door? I'm not gonna bat an eye. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're totally ignoring critical parts of my original post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, I see, you're going with &quot;only Exalts with a three-dot specialty in Hubris need apply.&quot; Feh. </div> </div> </div>If a Solar Exalt with Investigation, Lore and Occult Charms is NOT smarter than any mortal who ever lived, what IS he?<br /> <br /> If a Solar Exalt with those Charms is not smarter than even a scholarly Terrestrial or learned Sidereal, what IS he?<br /> <br /> &quot;The smartest man who ever lived&quot; is not a Lunar concept. That's not the story they're going to be designed to facilitate.<br /> <br /> Yes, they can be amazingly smart. A particular Lunar can be much smarter and more cunning and clever and educated than a particular Solar. But the Lunar's Charms are not going to tell the story of &quot;the smartest man to ever live&quot;; the Solar's Charms could.<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with Solar Exalted being the most powerful of them all, and all other Exalted needing to compare to the Solar Exalted, I don't think you're enjoying Exalted at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you even <i>like</i> Lunars? </div> </div> </div>Do you even like to argue in good faith?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm gonna go back to my ravens example. Ravens are smart. They can not only figure out tricks like bending a wire into a book to get a treat from a long-necked bottle, they can <i>teach each other tricks</i>. They can see our technology and use it to their benefit (dropping nuts in the crosswalk for cars to crack, then hitting the &quot;PRESS TO CROSS&quot; button to fly down and pick up their treat). </div> </div> </div>And a Lunar Exalt would scoff at our technology, and do it better than us. Because the Lunar is an Exalt, which means he is a human even before taking his Exalted power into account, and his Exalted power takes his strengths further.<br /> <br /> But whereas a Solar would express superhuman intelligence without thematic restrictions, thematic restrictions are the entire POINT of playing anything that isn't a Solar. A Lunar cannot do things like a Solar can do. There have to be some things the Lunar cannot do which the Solar could. Which means there needs to be a theme which limits what the Lunar can do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Like a bestial monster, but better than human&quot; seems both feasible and compelling. And that is how the Lunar would do technology better than us; like a bestial raven-god monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T22:43:55-08:00","id":330792,"title":"","content":"Hm. &quot;Like a bestial monster, but better than human&quot; applied to technology/intellectual pursuits make me think about things like Reaver tech, which would I suspect be more Abyssal/necromantic territory.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer &quot;mad genius&quot; or &quot;like an idiot savant&quot; or &quot;like an obsessive compulsive focused on this one thing&quot; for Lunars. I'd rather play up madness than animalistic stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:01:43-08:00","id":330797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330792#post330792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I prefer &quot;mad genius&quot; or &quot;like an idiot savant&quot; or &quot;like an obsessive compulsive focused on this one thing&quot; for Lunars. I'd rather play up madness than animalistic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heart's Blood, Lessons in the Blood, Intimate Training Recollection, Predator's Insight.<br /> <br /> There probably IS more than one avenue for Lunar super-intelligence, but &quot;like a monstrous beast&quot; is definitely one of them. Because Lunars eat people to learn what they knew.<br /> <br /> This thread is for compiling all of the &quot;smart monster&quot; examples that people have ever seen. It hasn't been very fruitful in that regard, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T23:27:21-08:00","id":330834,"title":"","content":"I don't like &quot;idiot savant&quot; because I don't want my genius character to be, well, an idiot.<br /> I prefer the bestial intelligence idea, but mad genius is fine too (and visions, and that sort of thing, which fits with the shamanic barbarian idea) since honestly, the Lunars are going to need a lot of thematic room to mine and make charms on. I don't think any one of these ideas is going to fill the Intelligence and Wits trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T09:40:46-08:00","id":331212,"title":"","content":"The one Lunar I ever did had a custom Intelligence charm that let him infer pertinent details the person he was talking to assumed he knew by extrapolating from their behavioural cues and his foreknowledge of the circumstances. ICly he developed it because he had an irritable, absent-minded mentor who would forget to tell him things and then get mad that he didn't know them, but I totally designed it as a power for helping you infiltrate in a stolen shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:08:04-08:00","id":331399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330792#post330792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. &quot;Like a bestial monster, but better than human&quot; applied to technology/intellectual pursuits make me think about things like Reaver tech, which would I suspect be more Abyssal/necromantic territory.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer &quot;mad genius&quot; or &quot;like an idiot savant&quot; or &quot;like an obsessive compulsive focused on this one thing&quot; for Lunars. I'd rather play up madness than animalistic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not going to go over well if we get a splat of the Neurodiversity Exalted. WW already had some irritating instances of &quot;Neurodiversity is Magic!&quot; in the classic WoD, such as with Demon and its &quot;autistic people have a weak connection to the soul and are thus meat puppets in waiting for any Demon that wants to snatch them&quot; nonsense. It'd be best to never walk down that road again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:04:33-08:00","id":331542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're glossing over the difference between mortal human intelligence and Exalted human intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm really not. Your dots don't somehow mean more just because you're the returning heroes of the dawn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you're totally ignoring critical parts of my original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, then, <i>First Age</i> door. Still, yawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Solar Exalt with Investigation, Lore and Occult Charms is NOT smarter than any mortal who ever lived, what IS he?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>As</i> smart as any mortal who ever lived. Sheesh, that really needed asking?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Solar Exalt with those Charms is not smarter than even a scholarly Terrestrial or learned Sidereal, what IS he?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>As</i> smart as a scholarly Terrestrial or learned Sidereal. Seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The smartest man who ever lived&quot; is not a Lunar concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. If ever I forget, remind me not to play any PbP games with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Lunar's Charms are not going to tell the story of &quot;the smartest man to ever live&quot;; the Solar's Charms could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> I'm going to quote pre-blasphemy-era George Lucas, here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Special effects are just a tool, a means of telling a story. People have a tendency to confuse them as an end to themselves. A Special effect without a story is a pretty boring thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's pretty obvious that he forgot this important lesson later in his life, but I think a very similar thing can be said here about Charms. Your Charms don't make you the smartest man to ever live any more than a guy with a bunch of Melee Charms gets to be the greatest swordsman who ever lived; it's a story he's gotta go out and earn for himself - the Charms aren't gonna do it for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a problem with Solar Exalted being the most powerful of them all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck, no. Power's a pretty nebulous thing in the first place, so Solars being on top doesn't really mean all that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=330765#post330765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and all other Exalted needing to compare to the Solar Exalted, I don't think you're enjoying Exalted at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pft. Whatever, man. I've got an Exalted game to run before I go into work tonight, so I'm going to stop here for now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:25:51-08:00","id":331563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331399#post331399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not going to go over well if we get a splat of the Neurodiversity Exalted. WW already had some irritating instances of &quot;Neurodiversity is Magic!&quot; in the classic WoD, such as with Demon and its &quot;autistic people have a weak connection to the soul and are thus meat puppets in waiting for any Demon that wants to snatch them&quot; nonsense. It'd be best to never walk down that road again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> In a setting with spirits and magic, where many of the superstitious explanations our cultures have developed for neurodivergent behavior (demonic possession, imbalance in the flows of energy within the body, the influence of the full moon's light, oracular visions, angelic visitations, possession by the divine, etc) are fact, though, it's odd for Lunars not to play with some of that superstitious imagery. We definitely should be trying to be sensitive about it, just as we try to be make sure the writing is dealing well with other problematic parts of the game's Pulp influences (slavery, prostitution, institutionalized oppression, depictions of sex or sexuality, etc), but I do feel the game loses something if the Chosen children of the goddess of madness can't don their patron's mantle.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd trust me to write powers like that in a way that keeps the cool old magicky feel but doesn't trivialize real-world conditions (or make them into bizarre supernatural weaknesses or superpowers). It's a tough tightrope to walk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T17:53:02-08:00","id":331636,"title":"","content":"Perhaps base it off the madness in stories rather than real madness.<br /> I mean, the classic mythical depiction of madness tends to have very little to do with schizophrenia, manic-depression.<br /> For example, multiple personalities is something which is very common in films but incredibly, incredibly rare in real life, compared to just the general erratic behaviour of a schizophrenic.<br /> Certainly the ecstatic visions of the Oracle of Delphi, shamanic cultures, etc, is something that would be appropriate and I don't think it's going to offend people.<br /> Obviously I can see why they need to be careful, but as you say, there's plenty of other controversial stuff and it hasn't broken the game (though I won't miss those discussions about Chapter 2 of Infernals).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T20:13:33-08:00","id":331797,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that there would be room for ecstasy and rage, if for no other reason than the cWoD game from which Lunars spring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:36:20-08:00","id":331897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm really not. Your dots don't somehow mean more just because you're the returning heroes of the dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, mate, I'm going to try laying this out again.<br /> <br /> A Solar's power is excellence; applying his excellence to intellectual pursuits make him smarter than mortal men. That's what Charms of Lore, Investigation, Occult and the like represent -- being smarter than mortal men can be (especially because qualifying for those Charms means you have the requisite dots to be at least as good as a mortal of the same capability). If mortal men could be so smart, they would have those Charms, or those Charms would be merely universal features of the basic system. Either way, the Solar Exalted wouldn't even exist.<br /> <br /> A Terrestrial's power is not pure excellence, but still elevates them above humanity in all 25 Abilities, because they are Ability-based Exalted and being elevated above the powers of mortal humanity is what Exaltation is all about. Like a Solar, a Terrestrial with dots and Charms of Lore is smarter than any mortal with the same number of dots, and situationally smarter than one with more dots.<br /> <br /> A Lunar's power is &quot;bestial monstrosity&quot;. Their most iconic ability is turning into animals, which is certainly &quot;monstrously bestial&quot;. People in Creation (especially in the Realm) can underestimate a Lunar's basic human intelligence on the assumption that turning into an animal curses you to be as dumb as one, and Lunars can feed this misunderstanding for all the advantage it is worth.<br /> <br /> You and I know that a Lunar is not any less intelligent than any other mortal human. But this tends to surprise people<i> in Creation</i>, who lack our meta-knowledge. What further surprises these fictional, subjectively-perspective people is that the Anathemic powers of &quot;beasts&quot; and &quot;monsters&quot; can be applied as much to mental capabilities as physical.<br /> <br /> So let us say there is a balanced Sworn Brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded mobilized in a Wyld Hunt against an old, powerful Lunar who balances physical and mental power. The Terrestrials see the Anathema fleeing and stalking and fighting them in the forms of beasts and monsters. She frequently doesn't look human, and maybe she doesn't even speak an intelligible language to them. They are faced with obvious signs of her physical power, but can easily begin to underestimate her intelligence.<br /> <br /> Remember that this is a balanced brotherhood. At least one of the Dragon-Blooded is an intellectual. He knows he is a true Exalt, the only kind of Exalt, a Prince of the Earth smarter than most of his Chosen peers, let alone the teeming mortal masses of humanity. Surely no barbarian peasant foolish enough to fall prey to demons could match wits with him, especially after the demons twisted her into a monstrous beast.<br /> <br /> But like I said, you and I know -- thanks to the Corebook and Lunar manual -- that this is not true. The Lunar knows this isn't true. Her Second Breath did not debase her, it Exalted her, and she has become far more insightful and cunning than ever before. In some ways, definitely more so than the learned member of the Terrestrial brotherhood.<br /> <br /> But not in all ways, because tiers are being tossed under a speeding bus. Terrestrials are going to have individual Lore, Investigation and Occult Charms which make them better at particular &quot;smart&quot; tasks than Lunar Charms can represent. Perhaps especially Crafting Charms.<br /> <br /> So, the question then becomes, in what manners are Lunars smarter than mortal humans? In what manners are they smarter than Terrestrials? In what matters are they as smart as Solars?<br /> <br /> In all the ways that ought to terrify a horror survival protagonist. It's a slasher movie, the Lunar is the monster, and the Terrestrials are the prey. The Terrestrials start out thinking the Lunar is stupid, but their Charm-represented cleverness and craftiness cannot protect them from her predation, because her Charm-representation cunning is too much for them. She figures out their magical locks, she has flashes of insight warning her about their magical traps, she recognizes how their magical weapons and defenses work and how to break them (or use them for herself), and she can eat any one of them to learn all of their plans and quirks. <br /> <br /> There are definitely other ways in which a Lunar can be superhumanly Intelligent! But this thread isn't for exploring those paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2014, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:41:14-08:00","id":331917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm really not. Your dots don't somehow mean more just because you're the returning heroes of the dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually precisely what they mean, those more dots you get with bonus points is because you're an Exalt. The difference between an Exalt and a mortal is not just their Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>As</i> smart as any mortal who ever lived. Sheesh, that really needed asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he has those charms and such specialized in them, he veritably is the smartest mortal living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>As</i> smart as a scholarly Terrestrial or learned Sidereal. Seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if the Exalt specializes in those charms, he veritably is smarter than them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. If ever I forget, remind me not to play any PbP games with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal attacks aren't necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to quote pre-blasphemy-era George Lucas, here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Special effects are just a tool, a means of telling a story. People have a tendency to confuse them as an end to themselves. A Special effect without a story is a pretty boring thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's pretty obvious that he forgot this important lesson later in his life, but I think a very similar thing can be said here about Charms. Your Charms don't make you the smartest man to ever live any more than a guy with a bunch of Melee Charms gets to be the greatest swordsman who ever lived; it's a story he's gotta go out and earn for himself - the Charms aren't gonna do it for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that they don't tell the story for you, but with specializing in those Charms, by skill and power alone the character is the smartest man or greatest swordsman who ever lived. They just need to prove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck, no. Power's a pretty nebulous thing in the first place, so Solars being on top doesn't really mean all that much.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>v<br /> While the power gaps are lessening, being on top still means quite a bit actually. They can be unparalleled sorcerers, wield a greater array of Evocations, currently have better XP economy in 2e. That's more of a difference that you think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:53:07-08:00","id":331921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that this is a balanced brotherhood. At least one of the Dragon-Blooded is an intellectual. He knows he is a true Exalt, the only kind of Exalt, a Prince of the Earth smarter than most of his Chosen peers, let alone the teeming mortal masses of humanity. Surely no barbarian peasant foolish enough to fall prey to demons could match wits with him, especially after the demons twisted her into a monstrous beast.<br /> <br /> But like I said, you and I know -- thanks to the Corebook and Lunar manual -- that this is not true. The Lunar knows this isn't true. Her Second Breath did not debase her, it Exalted her, and she has become far more insightful and cunning than ever before. In some ways, definitely more so than the learned member of the Terrestrial brotherhood. </div> </div> </div>Except actually the Dragonblood does know that the Lunar is probably as smart, if not smarter, than he is. The Wyld Hunt is effective because the Sidereals want it to work, and they know the Lunars are cunning. The Dragonblood think that the Lunars are disgusting monsters who stand against everything that is right and good in this world, but if the Sidereals let them think the Lunars were idiots, they'd get slaughtered. They well know that the Lunars might be extremely clever. Evil, but clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T22:59:45-08:00","id":331984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331921#post331921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except actually the Dragonblood does know that the Lunar is probably as smart, if not smarter, than he is. The Wyld Hunt is effective because the Sidereals want it to work, and they know the Lunars are cunning. The Dragonblood think that the Lunars are disgusting monsters who stand against everything that is right and good in this world, but if the Sidereals let them think the Lunars were idiots, they'd get slaughtered. They well know that the Lunars might be extremely clever. Evil, but clever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking of THE Wyld Hunt, I was thinking of <i>A</i> Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> A group of five Terrestrials with less collective experience than the Lunar they're hunting (so that the Lunar on her own can be equally and deeply invested in physical and mental capabilities) and the Terrestrial's mortal followers, who mobilized against a Lunar and called it a Wyld Hunt because that's what Dynasts call such an activity.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about an official mobilization of the Wyld Hunt as an Immaculate Institution, with support from the Legion and a Sidereal among the roster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T03:54:52-08:00","id":332103,"title":"","content":"Lunars, I hope, will fit concepts more like people uplifted to be holy god beasts or beast gods than bestial monsters.<br /> <br /> Like the Ki Rin or Loong or the conception of a yeti as a holy being. Creatures whose motifs can include above human wisdom, of which everyone in the setting would be aware, even if the Realm Dragonblooded would see it as anathema lies rather than wisdom.<br /> <br /> I feel like Lunars should not be obligate wearing badges or signifiers of mental or physical disease, mental incapacity, wrongness or terror, unless that's a choice their player makes. Also able to encompass beings with a physical difference from humanity, which is supernaturally beautiful, pure and healthy beyond people.<br /> <br /> Hoping we don't get moon mad Terrifying Argent Monsters. For all that maybe you can play one if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T05:47:10-08:00","id":332165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331984#post331984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't thinking of THE Wyld Hunt, I was thinking of <i>A</i> Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> A group of five Terrestrials with less collective experience than the Lunar they're hunting (so that the Lunar on her own can be equally and deeply invested in physical and mental capabilities) and the Terrestrial's mortal followers, who mobilized against a Lunar and called it a Wyld Hunt because that's what Dynasts call such an activity.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about an official mobilization of the Wyld Hunt as an Immaculate Institution, with support from the Legion and a Sidereal among the roster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Still, the DBs are generally very aware that Lunars are extremely dangerous.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while I see your point about the horror movies, and that might be fun, I don't see how the charms work. I don't see that building charms around assuming that the enemies the Lunar is fighting underestimate him works well, because sometimes they will, but sometimes they won't.<br /> Could you give some examples of the kind of thing you're going for? From the Lunars perspective, not the enemy's perspective, because that;s who the charms are being built for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the Ki Rin or Loong or the conception of a yeti as a holy being. Creatures whose motifs can include above human wisdom, of which everyone in the setting would be aware, even if the Realm Dragonblooded would see it as anathema lies rather than wisdom. </div> </div> </div>I like this idea, and it'd fit with what Hatewheel's view of what he wants Lunars to be, with all the mythic beats.<br /> <br /> Quite a lot of people have said &quot;they should be based on these themes&quot;, then others say &quot;no, these themes&quot;.<br /> I've got to be honest, considering how limited their mental charms have been, I'm entirely happy for their mental charms to fit into several different of the thematic sets that people have suggested. Bestial charms, mystic god-monster charms, Lunar as horror monster charms, insanity charms, dream charms, moon magic charms, I'm happy to have all of them. Now, it's important to have thematic limits because otherwise you have no theme at all... but I don't want to be playing a 650xp No Moon with a total of 4 Intelligence charms (including the excellency), because that's how almost all the interesting ones available, in the next edition.<br /> I'm more worried about lacking charms at all than having too vague a theme for them.<br /> Perhaps I'm underestimating the devs and then they can quite happily choose one very specific theme and then come up with 40 Int and Wits charms* out of it, but that's never happened in the past.<br /> <br /> *Perception is 95% fine as is. Plus it's really easy to come up with ideas for compared to the other areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T06:57:19-08:00","id":332183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=331542#post331542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. If ever I forget, remind me not to play any PbP games with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful with the personal attacks.<br /> <br /> Besides I think when he says that the smartest man alive isn't a Lunar concept he's talking about the splat as a whole.<br /> As a player character concept it's much more interesting for a Lunar to have this as their concept because their super intelligence is going to be filtered through shapeshifting and animal themed charms and looking for ways to hack their limitations while as a Solar it's not telling you much beyond the fact that they want to play a Twilight Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T08:00:33-08:00","id":332222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=332183#post332183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides I think when he says that the smartest man alive isn't a Lunar concept he's talking about the splat as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> I wasn't saying it was inappropriate for a player to try for that character concept, at least so long as he understands that the Lunar Exalted as a splat are not designed to facilitate that kind of story. Really, no one is but the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> And as Lioness says, that concept becomes more poignant for non-Solars precisely because of what it says about the character, and because of the greater challenge they face(d) in becoming the smartest human being alive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a player character concept it's much more interesting for a Lunar to have this as their concept because their super intelligence is going to be filtered through shapeshifting and animal themed charms and looking for ways to hack their limitations while as a Solar it's not telling you much beyond the fact that they want to play a Twilight Caste. </div> </div> </div>Exactly so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T09:29:14-08:00","id":332244,"title":"","content":"A Solar with Intelligence 5 and Lore 1 adds up to 6 dice with a Lore Excellency. He's educated AND smart.<br /> <br /> Also, quit splitting hairs over &quot;smart&quot; or &quot;educated&quot; when we're just throwing out a quick and easy term for &quot;Mental Attribute actions&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2014, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T10:04:38-08:00","id":332262,"title":"","content":"My favourite Lunar Intelligence charm of last edition was Perfect Outsider Understanding because it didn't feel obviously better suited to being a Lore or Occult charm due to the immediate practical applications of it that helped in combat and social situations too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T10:11:00-08:00","id":332266,"title":"","content":"Also, Solar Charms are based on Abilities but magnify related Attributes as well. It's why Lunar Charms are more complicated than &quot;more of the Attribute!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T10:44:48-08:00","id":332333,"title":"","content":"You could say a Solar who is the master of Lore isn't smarter than any mortal he just knows more and knows how to solve problems better. But how is that not being smarter? Being smarter *is* knowing more and being able to solve problems better.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not smarter. I just... know everything and can work out how anything works, by thinking. Faster and better than anyone else can.&quot; WTF? &quot;I'm not strong. I can just... lift anything because of how good I am at athletics&quot;. &quot;I'm not any more perceptive. I just have supernal awareness.&quot; &quot;My stamina is only normal. I just have enormous endurance&quot;. The abilities more or less encompass all the attributes, and extend them, in their scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T13:26:08-08:00","id":332468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying, that might be the point of contention-The Charms are not making the Solar More intellegent, they're making him more knowlegdable able and better able to use that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may simply be a matter of word choice than a real misunderstanding on your part, but I'll repeat what I said, which is what the developers have been telling us:<br /> <br /> &quot;Charms don't make you do anything. Charms represent your own abilities. You are not super-educated because you have Lore Charms, you have Lore Charms because you are super-educated. That's why Lore Charms require minimum ratings in the Lore Ability -- because they are extensions of your own human ability to act, not additional bits added or grown inside of you that enable to act.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alchemical Charms are the exception that prove the rule, what with being the only Charms that ARE additional bits built and added into you. Even then, your basic human(ish) body must be legendary enough that such capabilities belong in that body. You're never going to see a stupid Alchemical with a high-end Intelligence Charm. The fact that their artifact-Charms are not simply system abstractions is one of the defining traits of an Alchemical -- it's why they're the only ones whose Charms can be targeted and crippled through physical damage.<br /> <br /> Lunars also have Attribute Charms, but I'm not sure how those are going to be different from Alchemical Charms and everyone else's Ability-based Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Solar with INT 5 and Lore 1 is smart, but he's only mildly edjucated, which is comepnsated for becuase hi's charms mean, essentially, that he's magically more educated than an average mortal.<br /> <br /> a Lunar with INT 5 Lore 1, however, has Charms that give him intellect far above what mortal is capable of being, and that allow him to apply his superior intellect in ways that mortals just aren't capable of.<br /> <br /> Super Edjucated Solars, Super Smart Lunars. </div> </div> </div>Your example is woefully incomplete.<br /> <br /> What about comparing the <i>Intelligence 1, Lore 5</i> Solar against the <i>Intelligence 1, Lore 5</i> Lunar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:24:02-08:00","id":332500,"title":"","content":"So where does &quot;inherently smart&quot; go in terms of charms besides the excellency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:27:52-08:00","id":332501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, poor Word Choice, lore charms don't make the Solar supernaturally edjucated, he's got the charms becuase he's supernaturally edjucated. The Point is the Solar ins't Super Smart, he's Super Educated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can still boost Attributes with their Ability-based Charms. Increasing Strength Exercise exists and is likely not alone. Harmonious Academic Methodology also means that sufficiently educated Solars can Lawnmower Man themselves into more sophisticated mindsets. So much of the Solar milieu involves just being awesome in every way straightforwardly possible that it's not worth the time to try and split hairs this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-06-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T09:13:33-08:00","id":333030,"title":"","content":"Anyway building off of my fondness for Perfect Outsider Understanding.<br /> I think it'd be cool if you had an intellectually minded Lunar who used shapeshifting to be a sort of super ethologist who can experience animal behaviour in a way that nobody else can. So you'd pick a species of animals and the bonuses you got when dealing with them would also apply to the approrpiate spirits, beastfolk, other Lunars of the approrpiate totem etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T10:29:31-08:00","id":333202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=332500#post332500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So where does &quot;inherently smart&quot; go in terms of charms besides the excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the abstract (before getting down to mechanical brass tacks), anything an Intelligence charm can do is likely to be valid design space for some kind of Ability charm, but I think you can make some of those things <i>feel</i> more like Intelligence Charms, and the mechanical effects can reinforce that.<br /> <br /> It's not as dire a state of affairs as Stamina vs. Resistance or Perception vs. Awareness, happily. If I were going to pin down the difference between &quot;Intelligence&quot; and high ratings in knowledge abilities, I'd say it's that Intelligence represents a tireless, dynamic mind and a capacity for leaping insights and unexpected synergies. Feynman famously reduced most of the math involved into physics into a small set of elemental equations that could do everything, because he was extremely good at grasping, distilling, and repurposing the essence of complex systems. Being able to do that in the first place requires a firm grounding of the Ability, but it's an Intelligence task in itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T12:29:13-08:00","id":333284,"title":"","content":"Remembering stuff you never learned, learning stuff you didn't investigate, kenning sickness without education, designing feasible objects without training, seeing the best possible response a minute before something happens rather than planning hours ahead to know what was going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:16:24-08:00","id":333313,"title":"","content":"To be a naysayer, a lot of that does sound like &quot;So you're not using the Ability why now?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean I can see certain stories where you want to play a character who hasn't had formal or informal education (learning by doing probably being the main methodology for Solar heroes) and *hasn't* just bootstrapped up to, say, Medicine 4 or 5 using pure Exalted insight, but for the most part I think most people who want to be specifically good at those tasks will just be happy to have learning the Ability be in their backstory and go on to do more with them rather than use magic to cover that they haven't learnt them.<br /> <br /> Plus, perhaps also what the developers have said about it being cool to have Charms that have a logical means to them rather than which just give an answer or result?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T15:57:47-08:00","id":333526,"title":"","content":"Hey I'm not asking why doesn't the Lunar have Ability Charms, but whether using an Attribute Charm to substitute for not knowing an Ability will appeal to many character concepts or is a good logic overall.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have a Charm that lets me know the answer without learning!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's nice. Well done learning mystical techniques that allow you to succeed despite being totally ignorant! I just learnt about the subject and how to get to the answer. And now I have magic that lets me go beyond that answer.&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea of raft of Charms that let you get by the limitation of not knowing the relevant Ability if you want. <br /> <br /> It's just like the idea of a playing high Ability Solar who gets past his limitation of not having that high an Attribute by buying specific Charms. Wouldn't you just... buy the Attribute? <br /> <br /> And isn't it a weird incentive if the system encourages that Solar not to bother buying the Attribute or at least makes it experience neutral whether he does or does not?<br /> <br /> In the case of Lunars, is it a good thing to incentivize Lunar players not worrying about whether the build characters who cover their Abilities or whether their character is unskilled or ignorant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:30:32-08:00","id":333556,"title":"","content":"Maybe it'd be more effective to try and think in terms of the sort of characters we would imagine to be Lunars with high mental attribute stats.<br /> <br /> How about Bane, the Batman villain? We've been told 3E Lunars are extremely physical, and Bane certainly is, but a key part of his menace is that he is a very large, strong man who is also frightfully intelligent. In <i>The Dark Knight Rises</i> he stages a financial fraud by breaking into the trading floor and convincing everyone he's just there to rob the place. He is able to devise a path to escape pursuit despite Batman and the police having much faster vehicles. He has a meticulous attention to detail, as demonstrated by his staging of the death of the nuclear scientist (by something as low-tech as a last minute blood transfusion). He is able to coordinate a massive shadow organization's elaborate demolition project, striding through the earthworks and observing their efforts personally. He even manages a coup by acting in the exact moment when the people funneling him resources are at his mercy (&quot;Do you <i>feel </i>in charge?&quot;)<br /> <br /> All of these seem to display a very clever person who is simultaneously quite feral. What sort of charm concepts might indicate Bane-like intelligence? Or do you think Bane is a bad example of an intelligent Lunar-esque character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:30:49-08:00","id":333557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say a Solar who is the master of Lore isn't smarter than any mortal he just knows more and knows how to solve problems better. But how is that not being smarter? Being smarter *is* knowing more and being able to solve problems better.</div> </div> </div> </div> There were people as educated as Einstein who never could have figured out Relativity. There are educated people who lack a capacity for innovation and problem solving that less educated people are applying towards factors in their own context that may be less technically intricate but that are still improved upon by them. A fairly typical person can be taught how to assemble and service a spacecraft, while somewhere in the world there's a super genius of a subsistence farmer figuring out how to turn their limited resources towards notably improving crop yields or saving on labour. It's the difference between building a modern skyscraper and building Newgrange. It doesn't really have any pertinance to Exalted, but it's a good thing to keep in mind. for life in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:58:07-08:00","id":333568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333557#post333557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There were people as educated as Einstein who never could have figured out Relativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think someone else with his &quot;Physics&quot; Ability could've though (to the extent that Attributes and Abilities as realistic things which operate similarly to Exalted's even exist, which is not much).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333557#post333557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are educated people who lack a capacity for innovation and problem solving that less educated people are applying towards factors in their own context that may be less technically intricate but that are still improved upon by them. A fairly typical person can be taught how to assemble and service a spacecraft, while somewhere in the world there's a super genius of a subsistence farmer figuring out how to turn their limited resources towards notably improving crop yields or saving on labour. It's the difference between building a modern skyscraper and building Newgrange. It doesn't really have any pertinance to Exalted, but it's a good thing to keep in mind. for life in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of agree. I don't disagree with the general thrust. Although with the specific example of the subsistence farmer I think it is hard for me to imagine any sort of supergenius who wants to literally apply his genius in full, to perfecting the art of subsistence farming. Even if he's being compelled to do it, there's a certain point at which even a genius (of any sort of personality I find easy to imagine, which isn't ridiculously psychologically limited) goes &quot;It's just subsistence farming ffs&quot;.<br /> <br /> And if they're not being compelled* (by circumstances economic or direct pressure), and have any wherewithal to use their intellect, I expect they tend to be pretty soon not be doing subsistence farming.<br /> <br /> Either the mismatch of talent to task resolves itself, or it (sadly) doesn't but either way I feel like no one is investing exorbitant amounts of intellect in obsessively perfect versions of commonplace tasks.<br /> <br /> *on being compelled I think even very hierarchical societies of limited resources tend to go &quot;Obvious supergenius? We'll have some of that where we can best use it&quot;. *If* they're able to recognize it at all, which is probably much harder when lots of people's ability is only being tested against problems with a relatively low ceiling or a low power to be able to distinguish the quality of solutions (e.g. because there are too many uncontrolled factors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:59:59-08:00","id":333571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333556#post333556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it'd be more effective to try and think in terms of the sort of characters we would imagine to be Lunars with high mental attribute stats.<br /> <br /> How about Bane, the Batman villain? We've been told 3E Lunars are extremely physical, and Bane certainly is, but a key part of his menace is that he is a very large, strong man who is also frightfully intelligent. In <i>The Dark Knight Rises</i> he stages a financial fraud by breaking into the trading floor and convincing everyone he's just there to rob the place. He is able to devise a path to escape pursuit despite Batman and the police having much faster vehicles. He has a meticulous attention to detail, as demonstrated by his staging of the death of the nuclear scientist (by something as low-tech as a last minute blood transfusion). He is able to coordinate a massive shadow organization's elaborate demolition project, striding through the earthworks and observing their efforts personally. He even manages a coup by acting in the exact moment when the people funneling him resources are at his mercy (&quot;Do you <i>feel </i>in charge?&quot;)<br /> <br /> All of these seem to display a very clever person who is simultaneously quite feral. What sort of charm concepts might indicate Bane-like intelligence? Or do you think Bane is a bad example of an intelligent Lunar-esque character?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a Night Caste on dependence-forming drugs. He does what Batman does, and Batman is usually very Solar.<br /> <br /> Physically notable would perhaps be a better way to phrase Lunar physicality. Where a Solar is charming and well-versed in rhetoric, Lunars have inhuman voices that make others quiver and eyes like THE HYPNOTOAD. ALL HAIL THE HYPNOTOAD. They do know things by learning them, but their methods for learning include eating prey. The exceptionally clever fighters will no doubt derive sneaky tricks of legendary creatures, such as venom and other toxins, from their cleverness and cerebral nature. And they don't need to worry very much about Medicine, because if the working process of Lick Wound from 1e is any indication, they could just keep the injured close and clean their wounds with a beast-like tongue or with strange exhalations and poof, they're better. Granted, the mechanics of Lick Wound were terrible shit that even a cliath Garou fresh out of a Rite of Passage would feel sorry for the Lunars at having to deal with, but you have a speedbump up with Mother's Touch to describe where that sort of thing goes, so it's not like the notion that the Lunar heals by touching and imparting Essence is far-fatched. None of which, of course, is governed by the Medicine Ability as such. Technically, it doesn't even have to be related to Mental Attributes, either, but myth tends to attribute certain qualities to beasts based on what sorts of traits they show, and if venom is a sneaky trick, make the Charm that supplies venom require being clever.<br /> <br /> And no, given the context of Bane, not <i>that</i> venom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:47:07-08:00","id":333592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333571#post333571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's a Night Caste on dependence-forming drugs. He does what Batman does, and Batman is usually very Solar.<br /> <br /> Physically notable would perhaps be a better way to phrase Lunar physicality. Where a Solar is charming and well-versed in rhetoric, Lunars have inhuman voices that make others quiver and eyes like THE HYPNOTOAD. ALL HAIL THE HYPNOTOAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are perhaps characters we can argue to be non-Solars, but I think for the most part someone being representable as a Solar is not a good metric by which to disqualify them as an example for other splats, otherwise all non-Solars would have rather slim narrative pickings.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you don't think Bane is a good example of an intelligent Lunar, who is? Can you give me an example of a character in a story who has Hypnotoad powers, say, but is a bit more fleshed out as someone you'd actually play as a PC than Hypnotoad? Or a character with the other sorts of abilities you describe, whose personal story resembles the sort you'd expect a PC Lunar to have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:22:44-08:00","id":333641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333592#post333592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are perhaps characters we can argue to be non-Solars, but I think for the most part someone being representable as a Solar is not a good metric by which to disqualify them as an example for other splats, otherwise all non-Solars would have rather slim narrative pickings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bane is quite well-realized in his setting as a normally formidable person rubbing elbows with characters that are literally supermonsters. I don't think that I'm edging out too many concepts if I say that he's probably not a good example of a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, if you don't think Bane is a good example of an intelligent Lunar, who is? Can you give me an example of a character in a story who has Hypnotoad powers, say, but is a bit more fleshed out as someone you'd actually play as a PC than Hypnotoad? Or a character with the other sorts of abilities you describe, whose personal story resembles the sort you'd expect a PC Lunar to have? </div> </div> </div>(As a heads up, I was mentioning many different Attributes there. The Hypnotoad is more in the bounds of Charisma and Manipulation.)<br /> <br /> First comes the &quot;monster with good person inside, or good person with monster inside&quot; marriage of opposite internal traits. Then comes the selective Kagerou-ing, or being an unnamed cannibal shaman in Yu YuHakusho or what have you. We've pretty much already established that a lot of Charms that involve being clever could likely fall under other Mental Attributes. If you know that power runs through a facility and have some means to perceive this directly, it's not a really a huge leap to notice that the places that don't have the buzzing also don't have functional lighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T22:21:49-08:00","id":333792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=333526#post333526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey I'm not asking why doesn't the Lunar have Ability Charms, but whether using an Attribute Charm to substitute for not knowing an Ability will appeal to many character concepts or is a good logic overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dexterity attack Charm does not substitute for Melee or any other attack Ability. But it needs to be able to function even when you have absolutely no training whatsoever, or else it's just an Ability Charm posing as an Attribute Charm.<br /> <br /> An Attribute Charm should never NEED an Ability score, though the best should still benefit from an Ability score.<br /> <br /> Avoiding Silver Solar Intelligence Charms is really hard unless you design against the possibility that the Lunar has absolutely no dots in Lore, Investigation or whatever Ability is relevant to the Charm's purpose. In fact, designing with that goal in mind should definitely produce sufficiently inhuman results that lend towards a uniquely &quot;Lunar&quot; experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> By contrast, Ability Charms may always assume that the Exalt has at least one dot in the relevant Attribute, because there are generally never any rolls which do not combine (Attribute + Ability) for a dice-pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:27:10-08:00","id":776297,"title":"","content":"Responding to a post from another thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/775260-lunar-charms-we-want-to-see?p=775411#post775411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you still wanting to do that one where the Lunar puts people in awe of her clever door-opening skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you still going to be so appallingly immature, hostile, and close-minded?<br /> <br /> Grow up.<br /> <br /> Is &quot;passive-aggressive&quot; the proper way to describe this comment's childishness? I tell you truly, it was &quot;passive-aggressive&quot; enough that I didn't even have a clue what you were talking about until a few hours later and a second reading. In part because you didn't have the guts or the courtesy to address me by name or by quote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm to take your backbiting at face-value, then you still haven't even bothered trying to understand what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> Which is justifying the Lunars getting a Charm like or somehow on par with the Solar Larceny Charms, Lock-Opening Touch and Door-Evading Technique in the backer's draft, on the basis that animals can be really good at breaking into places.<br /> <br /> Of course no mere raccoon can break into sorcerously locked and barred vaults of long-dead First Age Solars, but Lunar Exalted are no mere raccoons, just as they are no mere men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2015, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:18:03-08:00","id":776337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776314-lunars?p=776316#post776316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that one of those threads was necro'd from a year after it started because its author wanted to diss someone who mentioned it offhandedly in another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanted to pick a fight.<br /> <br /> I revived the old thread to move the argument back into a more appropriate place.<br /> <br /> Also, why don't you claim responsibility?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:20:39-08:00","id":776340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776337#post776337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wanted to pick a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:25:56-08:00","id":776345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776340#post776340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>If not derision, what tone do you think you conveyed with the words, &quot;Are you still wanting to do that one where the Lunar puts people in awe of her clever door-opening skills?&quot;<br /> <br /> And if nothing other than derision was your intent, what schoolyard did you grow up on, where badmouthing didn't invite a fight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:26:38-08:00","id":776347,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> the problem of Lunar Charms, that you seem to be talking about Sunder, is that its kind of hard in general to figure out what Intelligence is absent of education. we-as a civilization- don't have many examples, because we associate education and intelligence together pretty strongly. mostly because the most intelligent characters and heroes we know are probably well-educated to show how intelligent they are, because the things you get education on, are probably pretty complex.<br /> <br /> though you might have something to the direction of these charms, of being a beast who figures things out and does stuff that you don't expect savage barbarian beastly things to do, sounds like a good direction to go. <br /> <br /> I guess a Lore 1, Intelligence 5 character would be someone who doesn't know much but can rapidly figure out more information when the evidence is presented to them and logically piece things together in their head from what they can reasonably assume<br /> <br /> while the inverse, a Lore 5, Intelligence 1 character would be someone who is very slow to figure things out, but has trained himself to memorize so much information and such that he seems smart because he worked really hard to be able to memorize and retain all of it, and thus would be really dependent upon what he already knows to fix the problem.<br /> <br /> so I guess a lot of Lunar Intelligence charms by such a definition would be rapidly figuring things out in their head from what information they already know. knowing more stuff would be a problem for Perception charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:29:43-08:00","id":776349,"title":"","content":"Raziere, thank you so much. You made me so happy.<br /> <br /> You not only actually read and considered my posts, you responded with a thoughtful and on-topic analysis!<br /> <br /> Also, that does sound like where I see Lunar Lore/Investigation Charms going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:36:44-08:00","id":776352,"title":"","content":"I didn't grow up on a schoolyard, for the record.<br /> <br /> That said, my problem was never with Lunars having equivalents of Lock-Opening Technique, but rather this notion you put forward from the opening post on that folks in Creation would assume them to be animal-minded monsters when Lunars are and have always been human and specifically have an entire caste of them even noted in-universe by their fixation on the mental Attributes. <br /> <br /> Muldoon's &quot;Clever girl&quot; and Hudson's &quot;How could they cut the power, man? They're animals!&quot; only made sense because the characters thought that the opposition was of animal-level intelligence - if it had been humans instead of velociraptors and xenomorphs, someone would've backhanded Hudson for being a dumbass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:42:29-08:00","id":776356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776352#post776352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Muldoon's &quot;Clever girl&quot; and Hudson's &quot;How could they cut the power, man? They're animals!&quot; only made sense because the characters thought that the opposition was of animal-level intelligence - if it had been humans instead of velociraptors and xenomorphs, someone would've backhanded Hudson for being a dumbass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that the velociraptors weren't animals, or were somehow smarter than animals?<br /> <br /> I think they were just animals, and even though Muldoon knew how smart they were, even he was taken by surprise by their animal cunning.<br /> <br /> By the same token, couldn't a Wyld Hunter know that a Lunar Anathema is not actually JUST an animal, and still be taken by surprise at how crafty they are at disabling traps, laying ambushes, and getting past locks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:54:11-08:00","id":776361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776356#post776356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that the velociraptors weren't animals, or were somehow smarter than animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an animal sitting at your computer, and one at mine, too. That said, the phrase &quot;animal intelligence&quot; is generally taken to mean &quot;less than human intelligence,&quot; regardless of the accuracy of the phrase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776356#post776356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, couldn't a Wyld Hunter know that a Lunar Anathema is not actually JUST an animal, and still be taken by surprise at how crafty they are at disabling traps, laying ambushes, and getting past locks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I'd think it's a different kind of surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:55:42-08:00","id":776363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776352#post776352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't grow up on a schoolyard, for the record.<br /> <br /> That said, my problem was never with Lunars having equivalents of Lock-Opening Technique, but rather this notion you put forward from the opening post on that folks in Creation would assume them to be animal-minded monsters when Lunars are and have always been human and specifically have an entire caste of them even noted in-universe by their fixation on the mental Attributes.<br /> <br /> Muldoon's &quot;Clever girl&quot; and Hudson's &quot;How could they cut the power, man? They're animals!&quot; only made sense because the characters thought that the opposition was of animal-level intelligence - if it had been humans instead of velociraptors and xenomorphs, someone would've backhanded Hudson for being a dumbass.</div> </div> </div> </div>....um....just a thought: there is an entire religious order going around spreading propaganda about the Lunars and calling them demons and you know, generally reinforcing prejudice against them.<br /> <br /> and prejudice has been known to make people have stupid assumptions about other people. when people think of another group as subhuman.....they tend not to take into account any evidence that could suggest that they are not subhuman, such as y'know....actually being able to figure out stuff they can. I mean....a lot of prejudice in the past were based on the civilization assuming that because it accomplished something and no one else did (see China, Egypt, Rome, colonial/imperial Europe and so on and so forth) that they were somehow more intelligent than the other civilizations around them.<br /> <br /> so its not that hard for me to believe that the Immaculate Order has been going around reinforcing the belief that Lunars are stupid barbarians who couldn't possibly figure out how things like the Realm works through propaganda, because &quot;they turn into animals, therefore they must be STUPID like them see?&quot; and people would buy it because its a reassuring lie that makes them feel superior for not being possessed by some silver demon that makes you stupid like an animal, and thus gives them better reason to attack them, because then they don't have to consider whether or not they are intelligent enough to be reasoned with. <br /> <br /> so unless you want the Immaculate Order to tell the truth and make in-setting people actually scared of the Lunars, thus....hindering the Immaculate Order...I don't see your logic. I mean sure the Immaculate Order and the Sidereals probably knows better than to believe their own lies, but who said that anyone else has to?<br /> <br /> so yeah....this whole train of thought seems right up Exalted's ally really...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:55:58-08:00","id":776364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/323495-that-s-not-fair-monsters-shouldn-t-be-so-smart-discussing-lunar-intelligence?p=776347#post776347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.<br /> <br /> the problem of Lunar Charms, that you seem to be talking about Sunder, is that its kind of hard in general to figure out what Intelligence is absent of education. we-as a civilization- don't have many examples, because we associate education and intelligence together pretty strongly. mostly because the most intelligent characters and heroes we know are probably well-educated to show how intelligent they are, because the things you get education on, are probably pretty complex.<br /> <br /> though you might have something to the direction of these charms, of being a beast who figures things out and does stuff that you don't expect savage barbarian beastly things to do, sounds like a good direction to go.<br /> <br /> I guess a Lore 1, Intelligence 5 character would be someone who doesn't know much but can rapidly figure out more information when the evidence is presented to them and logically piece things together in their head from what they can reasonably assume<br /> <br /> while the inverse, a Lore 5, Intelligence 1 character would be someone who is very slow to figure things out, but has trained himself to memorize so much information and such that he seems smart because he worked really hard to be able to memorize and retain all of it, and thus would be really dependent upon what he already knows to fix the problem.<br /> <br /> so I guess a lot of Lunar Intelligence charms by such a definition would be rapidly figuring things out in their head from what information they already know. knowing more stuff would be a problem for Perception charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another direction to go in. In the cWoD, spirits in Werewolf didn't have Attributes or Abilities - just Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower. The latter two were used to determine a spirit's facility with mental and social actions, How much a spirit could guess or &quot;reason&quot; about a subject was based on its connection to the greater whole of the cosmos (Gnosis), while thinking on its feet was down to its sense of RESOLVE! (Willpower). There were no Trait pairs to add up; it was just that Trait, which typically ranged from 1 to 10 (though some spirits broke those standards over their knee, like the Rage 20 and Willpower 15 of Fenris's war-avatar, or the death-spirits known as the Maidens of Styx having Gnosis 17).<br /> <br /> So instead of representing how &quot;smart&quot; or &quot;clever&quot; you are, extensions of those Attributes in the Lunar corner might tap into primal wellsprings of revelatory knowledge and certainty. Depth of thought gets turned into the capacity to tear through boundaries of what one has experienced personally, studied, or heard from gossip. Which is pretty close to how 1e's Lore-Speaking Method worked, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}